<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hattin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1187">1187</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Hattin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Hattin was fought in 1187 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberias">Tiberias</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galilee">Galilee</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> and the army of the Crusader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a>. Saladin destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader</a> army and captured its king. The victory allowed him to retake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> later that year and is the defining military triumph of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin.jpg" alt="Battle of Hattin" width="320" height="138" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matthew Paris · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saladin_Guy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Battle of Hattin</b> on 4 July 1187 was the culmination of this strategy: by drawing the Crusader army out from the springs of Sephoria into waterless terrain at the height of summer and denying it access to the Sea of Galilee, Saladin forced the entire field army…</blockquote><a href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>At the <b>Battle of Hattin</b> on 4 July 1187, Saladin surrounded and destroyed the army of King Guy of Lusignan, perhaps 20,000 men, cut off from water near Lake Tiberias.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>His son Muzaffar al-Din Gökböri married Rabi'a Khatun, sister of Saladin, fought at the <b>Battle of Hattin</b> in 1187 and received Erbil as an Ayyubid ally in 1190.</blockquote><a href="/state/begteginid-dynasty">Begteginid dynasty</a></li><li><blockquote>Raynald was executed by Saladin after the battle of <b>Hattin</b> in 1187.</blockquote><a href="/state/lordship-of-oultrejordain">Lordship of Oultrejordain</a></li><li><blockquote>The royal army marched to relieve her and was destroyed at <b>Hattin</b>, and Galilee fell to Saladin.</blockquote><a href="/state/principality-of-galilee">Principality of Galilee</a></li></ul></section>
